---
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Kicker from '../Kicker.astro';

interface Props {
  title?: string;
}
const { title = 'The datacentre is yours.' } = Astro.props;

// Argument from Peter Wilson, "AI Growth Zones: gift horse or Trojan horse?" (2026).
const POST =
  'https://peteski22.github.io/blog/2026/02/04/ai-growth-zones-gift-horse-or-trojan-horse/';
const rows = [
  [
    'Who owns it',
    'Big tech companies and their investors, mostly American: Microsoft, Google, Amazon, OpenAI and the like',
    'Your local library, co-op or neighbours',
  ],
  [
    'Where the money goes',
    'To shareholders, mostly in the US',
    'Stays local: running costs and local jobs',
  ],
  ['Where your data goes', 'Wherever they send it', "Nowhere you haven't agreed to"],
  [
    'What your area gets',
    'Noise, and more demand for power and water',
    'Skills, jobs and a say in how it runs',
  ],
  ['Who decides', 'Their boards and investors', 'Members'],
];
---

<Section tone="soil" id="datacentre" labelledby="dc-title">
  <Kicker>Community-owned compute</Kicker>
  <h2 id="dc-title">{title}</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Big AI datacentres are being built near towns like ours. The town gets the noise and the extra
    demand for power and water. The profits, and the data, mostly go to a handful of large American
    tech companies.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">
    Freehold turns that around. A node in your local library, co-op or village hall is a datacentre
    your community owns, runs and decides about.
  </p>
  <table>
    <caption class="visually-hidden">Their datacentre compared with your community node</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <td></td>
        <th scope="col" class="mono">
          Their datacentre
        </th>
        <th scope="col" class="mono ours">
          Your community node
        </th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {rows.map(([k, theirs, ours]) => (
        <tr>
          <th scope="row" class="mono">
            {k}
          </th>
          <td data-label="Their datacentre">{theirs}</td>
          <td data-label="Your community node" class="ours">
            {ours}
          </td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <figure class="quote">
    <blockquote>A datacentre can be bought back one day. Your data can't.</blockquote>
    <figcaption>
      Adapted from <a href={POST}>AI Growth Zones: gift horse or Trojan horse?</a> by Peter Wilson
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</Section>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 0.5vw + 1rem, 1.2rem);
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(246 239 228 / 20%);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  thead th {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--chalk);
  }
  tbody th {
    color: var(--sun-light);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }
  .ours {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  thead .ours {
    color: var(--sun-light);
  }
  .quote {
    margin: var(--space-7) 0 0;
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw + 0.8rem, 2.1rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--clay);
    max-width: 24ch;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    thead {
      display: none;
    }
    tr,
    th,
    td {
      display: block;
    }
    tr {
      padding-block: var(--space-3);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(246 239 228 / 20%);
    }
    th,
    td {
      border: 0;
      padding: var(--space-1) 0;
    }
    td::before {
      content: attr(data-label) ': ';
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      opacity: 0.8;
    }
  }
</style>
